# The two origins a deployment answers at, and the only file that holds them.
# Compose hands it to the containers (`env_file` in docker-compose.yml) and to
# the web image's build (Dockerfile.web bakes the API origin into the browser
# bundle); nothing else reads it. A checkout's `.env` carries the same two keys
# with its own values — this box is a deploy target as well as a checkout, so
# one file for both is a dev server serving the deployed origins or a deployment
# serving loopback.
#
# The name is the other half of that: vite and bun load `.env`, `.env.local` and
# `.env.<mode>`, and never a name shaped like this one, so no dev run can pick a
# deployed origin up whatever mode it is in.
#
# Origins only, and that is a contract rather than a habit: every key here is
# one a checkout's env may then name nowhere but this machine, so a deployment
# variable that is not an origin — a DSN, a token, a feature flag — belongs in
# docker-compose.yml under the service that reads it, and scripts/origins.ts
# refuses this file if one lands here.
#
# No secrets here either — the same two public names
# infra/nginx/project-template.conf serves, which is what
# scripts/env-wiring.test.ts holds them to. scripts/preview.sh writes a file of
# this shape for the preview stack, which is why compose takes the name from
# ORIGINS_ENV rather than spelling this one out.
SITE_URL=https://project-template.example.com
PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.project-template.example.com
